43. The principles governing the grant of leave to appeal may be summarised as under:
i. Sections 96 and 100 of the CPC respectively provide for preferring an appeal from
an original decree or decree in appeal respectively;
ii. The said provisions do not enumerate the categories of persons who can file an
appeal;
iii. However, it a settled legal proposition that a stranger cannot be permitted to file
an appeal in any proceedings unless he satisfies the court that he falls within the
category of an aggrieved person;
iv. It is only where a judgment and decree prejudicially affects a person who is not a
party to the proceedings, he can prefer an appeal with the leave of the court;
v. A person aggrieved, to file an appeal, must be one whose right is affected by reason
of the judgment and decree sought to be impugned;
vi. The expression “person aggrieved” does not include a person who suffers from a
psychological or an imaginary injury;

